+</div></header><main id="main"><div class="wrap"><p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Announcements archive</p><div class="news-archive vap-news"><div class="archive-hero"><span class="archive-eyebrow">VAP · NEWS ARCHIVE</span><h1>Announcements archive</h1><p>VAP research and website update history.</p></div><aside class="news-status"><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI and saved-evidence checks are distinct from independent fresh execution.</p></aside><p class="archive-history-label">Dates below are original publication dates. Later updates are identified when recorded. Historical notices describe the status at that time; their claims are not new confirmations of adoption, conformance or certification.</p><form class="archive-controls" hidden><label>Month<select name="month"><option value="">All</option><option value="2026-11">2026-11</option><option value="2026-10">2026-10</option></select></label><label class="archive-search">Search announcements<input type="search" name="search" autocomplete="off"></label><input type="hidden" name="category" value=""><button type="reset">Reset filters</button></form><p class="archive-count" id="archive-count" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-template="{shown} of {total} records">9 of 9 records</p><p class="archive-empty" id="archive-empty" hidden>No announcements match these filters.</p><section class="archive-month" id="month-2026-11"><h2>2026-11</h2><ul class="news-list"><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261102" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-02">2026-11-02</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Evidect #30–#34 add synthetic permission and receiver-state experiments. Latest first-party CI passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS job. Extensions remain unadopted; independent…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261102-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261102" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</h2><p>Evidect #30–#34 add service-permission rechecks, saved ten-case verification, checkpoint expiry/generations/key revocation and challenge-bound checks against a separate store. Latest merged eeeacf7 passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS first-party CI job (44 new + 262 existing).</p><p>These are same-controller synthetic experiments. Separate processes and keys do not establish independent administration; both-store rollback and other limits remain. Extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. The 137-test record, earlier results and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">Read the five updates and their limits →</a></p></section>
+</div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261101" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-01">2026-11-01</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-01-runtime-handoff-incident-review/">1 November: saved-report receiver verification and incident review</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Evidect #28 adds receiver verification; #29 documents incident sources and scope limits. First-party CI passed 137 tests and eight synthetic cases per OS. Extensions remain…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261101-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261101" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">1 November: saved-report receiver verification and incident review</h2><p>Evidect #28 binds the signed observation handoff to original report bytes and recomputes summaries from saved observations. Each Ubuntu/macOS first-party CI passed 137 tests, including 27 new tests, and eight synthetic cases. PR #29 documents incident sources and scope limits; its three future test candidates remain unimplemented and untested.</p><p>Saved-evidence verification does not rerun the original operation or re-establish its authorization and original signatures. A narrow VALID is not a safety verdict. Extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Historical 53-case, 159 / 26 and other records and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-01-runtime-handoff-incident-review/">Read the two updates and their limits →</a></p></section>
+</div></details></div></li></ul></section><section class="archive-month" id="month-2026-10"><h2>2026-10</h2><ul class="news-list"><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261031" data-news-record data-month="2026-10" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-31">2026-10-31</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-31-retention-runtime-interop-research-update/">31 October follow-up: post-approval changes, retention evidence and interoperability</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Three research areas: Evidect post-approval checks and process observations, VAP/Evidect retention review, and Python/Node interoperability. First-party CI only; extensions remain…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261031-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261031" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">31 October follow-up: post-approval changes, retention evidence and interoperability</h2><p>Evidect #27 tests post-approval changes and process observations (37 existing + 43 new tests; eight synthetic cases). VAP #39–#41 and Evidect #22–#26 separate retention deadlines, deletion evidence and receiver review. VAP #1 adds Python/Node interoperability (32 test methods; two positive and six negative vectors). First-party CI counts remain separate by scope.</p><p>Process separation is not independent authority; a reached deadline or CLOSED_REVIEW does not establish deletion success. Proposals and experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Historical 53-case, 159 / 26 and other records and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-31-retention-runtime-interop-research-update/">Read the three research areas and limits →</a></p></section>
+</div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261030-evening" data-news-record data-month="2026-10" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-30">2026-10-30</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-30-evidence-preservation-collector-review-update/">30 October follow-up: evidence preservation, rechecks and guide notices</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP #33 binds publication, disclosure and authorization; #34 covers scoped erasure; #35 preserves 53 original evidence cases and an offline kit; #36 generates bilingual reports;…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261030-evening-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261030-evening" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">30 October follow-up: evidence preservation, rechecks and guide notices</h2><p>VAP #33 binds publication, disclosure and authorization; #34 covers scoped erasure; #35 preserves 53 original evidence cases and an offline kit; #36 generates bilingual reports; #37 maps 23 requirements and provides review handoff; #38 checks sending prerequisites during collector outage and recovery. VCP guide #3 and #4 distinguish illustrative SDK names from the available SDK, and historical certification procedures from VSO’s current role.</p><p>Runtime checks passed first-party Python 3.12 / 3.14 CI. Saved-evidence rechecks are not fresh runs; automated reports are not human review. Proposals and extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Erasure is not universal deletion; collector evidence is not independent observation or all-route bypass prevention. Historical tests and fixed distributions remain intact.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-30-evidence-preservation-collector-review-update/">Read the eight updates and limits →</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261030" data-news-record data-month="2026-10" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-30">2026-10-30</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-30-incident-evidence-authorization-research-update/">30 October: evidence assessment, uploads and authorization research</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP PR #30 proposes evidence bindings; #31 provides an offline assessor (20 test methods; 23/23 matching scenarios); #32 exercises loopback uploads (39 methods; 17/17 upload cases…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261030-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261030" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">30 October: evidence assessment, uploads and authorization research</h2><p>VAP PR #30 proposes evidence bindings; #31 provides an offline assessor (20 test methods; 23/23 matching scenarios); #32 exercises loopback uploads (39 methods; 17/17 upload cases and 17/17 evidence rechecks match). Evidect #20 adds a synthetic authorization gate (37 tests; 18 scenarios); #21 adds optional SQLite replay reservations (33 new tests; 70 gate-specific tests and four process scenarios). Counts remain separate by scope.</p><p>All results are first-party CI checks. Upload case UL-14 shows a <strong>successful bypass outside the gate</strong>, not OS isolation or production bypass prevention. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Historical 159 / 26 and 306 / 140 test records and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-30-incident-evidence-authorization-research-update/">Read the five updates and limits →</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261029" data-news-record data-month="2026-10" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-29">2026-10-29</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-29-sdk-evidence-demo-reproduction-update/">VSO updates SDK evidence checks, the Explorer demo and Evidect reproduction guidance</a></h3><p class="news-summary">29 October: stricter SDK inputs, an API-connected signed-evidence Explorer route and Evidect reproduction guidance are available. The legacy dashboard and historical 159 / 26 and…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261029-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261029" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">VSO updates SDK evidence checks, the Explorer demo and Evidect reproduction guidance</h2><p>29 October: stricter SDK inputs, an API-connected signed-evidence Explorer route and Evidect reproduction guidance are available. The legacy dashboard and historical 159 / 26 and 306 / 140 test records remain separate. Experimental extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>.</p><p>The new demo uses signed synthetic evidence; intact full evidence is still INDETERMINATE. The API-disconnected / unsigned description in the 27 October record applies to the legacy dashboard.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-29-sdk-evidence-demo-reproduction-update/">Read the update and limits →</a> · <a href="https://veritaschain.org/explorer/app/#/evidence-demo">SDK Evidence Demo</a> · <a href="https://evidect.veritaschain.org/methodology/#reproduce">Evidect</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261028" data-news-record data-month="2026-10" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-28">2026-10-28</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-28-vap-lap-sdk-status-update/">VSO updates VAP-LAP references, VAP errata and SDK boundary checks</a></h3><p class="news-summary">28 October: VAP-LAP proposal links, current Draft 3 errata/hash references and SDK boundary checks are available. SDK first-party CI passed 306 Python and 140 TypeScript tests per…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261028-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261028" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">VSO updates VAP-LAP references, VAP errata and SDK boundary checks</h2><p>28 October: VAP-LAP proposal links, current Draft 3 errata/hash references and SDK boundary checks are available. SDK first-party CI passed <strong>306 Python and 140 TypeScript tests per matrix job</strong>, including 13 shared cases and 15 focused tests per language. The Explorer 159-test notice below is retained separately. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction has <strong>not been established</strong>.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-28-vap-lap-sdk-status-update/">Read the update and limits →</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="explorer-update-20261027" data-news-record data-month="2026-10" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-27">2026-10-27</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-report-intake-explorer-update/#explorer-update-20261027">27 October: Explorer API&#x27;s 159 tests and public GUI update</a></h3><p class="news-summary">The separate Explorer API fixed search-filter validation and exact nanosecond time-range comparisons. Its first-party CI passed 159 tests , with zero failures, cancellations,…</p><details class="archive-record" id="explorer-update-20261027-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-explorer-update-20261027" class="status" aria-label="Explorer update — 27 October 2026"><h2 style="margin-top:0">27 October: Explorer API's 159 tests and public GUI update</h2><p>The separate Explorer API fixed search-filter validation and exact nanosecond time-range comparisons. Its first-party CI passed <strong>159 tests</strong>, with zero failures, cancellations, skips or TODOs. This is a repository/CI checkpoint, not confirmation of a production API deployment.</p><p>The <a href="https://veritaschain.org/explorer/app/">public Explorer GUI</a> now requires an explicit tree size for its inclusion calculation, handles uneven branches and rejects malformed proofs. The GUI's separate first-party suite passed <strong>26 tests</strong>. The public page remains an API-disconnected demo with 12 synthetic leaves: unsigned, externally unanchored, and not hashes derived from the displayed event contents. A path matching a supplied root does not authenticate the root or tree size, or verify event contents, signatures or external anchors.</p><p>First-party publication checks exercised the 12 demo inclusion controls, notice placement at seven widths, and mobile controls. These checks are separate from the 159 API tests and <strong>do not establish independent reproduction</strong>. VAP's historical teaching snippets and the fixed RTA review target remain separate. VAP is still Draft 3; experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain <strong>unadopted</strong>, and independent third-party reproduction has <strong>not been established</strong>.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-report-intake-explorer-update/#explorer-update-20261027">Detailed update and limits</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-explorer-api/actions/runs/40355875498">API CI: 159 tests</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-explorer-gui/actions/runs/40360033313">GUI CI: 26 tests</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-site/actions/runs/40427147021">First-party public-page checks</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="status-update-20261026" data-news-record data-month="2026-10" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-26">2026-10-26</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-rta-verifier-checkpoint/">GitHub and status update — 26 October 2026</a></h3><p class="news-summary">RTA verifier review checkpoint: the separate VCP RTA repository now provides fixes and a fixed review target ( cc695fe ). Recorded first-party CI passed 809 regression and 15…</p><details class="archive-record" id="status-update-20261026-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><aside class="status" aria-label="GitHub and status update"><strong>GitHub and status update — 26 October 2026</strong><p><strong>RTA verifier review checkpoint:</strong> the separate VCP RTA repository now provides fixes and a fixed review target (<code>cc695fe</code>). Recorded first-party CI passed 809 regression and 15 separate historical tests per environment, while the 40-event evidence replay remains <strong>INDETERMINATE</strong>. This does not establish independent reproduction, full conformance or a new release. <a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-rta-verifier-checkpoint/">Read the RTA update and limits →</a> A <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/actions/runs/40263948191">separate first-party CI</a> also completed the unchanged published recipe from a fresh network clone through final assessment on Python 3.11 and 3.13.5; this is procedure validation, not independent reproduction.</p><p>The <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-spec/pull/16">VCP candidate schema and synthetic checker</a> and <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/pull/26">VAP three-valued verification proposal</a> have been incorporated as research. Experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain <strong>unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established</strong>. VAP v1.2.0 is still Draft 3. VCP v1.2 is Released, with known integrity issues under review and full conformance to VAP unestablished. This website's code examples are not a native VCP conformance verifier.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-sdk/releases/tag/v0.1.0">vcp-sdk v0.1.0</a> is a first-party pre-release offline core on GitHub, not a PyPI/npm release, an implementation of vcp-sdk-spec, or an independent external implementation. Its interpretation choices do not adopt normative changes.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/blob/81fa81e01ef9418c3fb7a02ddfc7fd72d993b6b1/README.md#implementation-status-mandatory-disclosure">VSO's published disclosure as of 25 October 2026</a> reports zero external implementations and zero Evidence Packs accepted in proceedings. These are disclosed project counts, not an independent assessment. <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/blob/81fa81e01ef9418c3fb7a02ddfc7fd72d993b6b1/disclosures/2026-10-24-commercial-contracts.md">Earlier commercial figures remain withdrawn pending verification</a>; this is not a zero-contract finding. Current normative requirements, existing implementations, signed data, fixed distributions and K3 are unchanged by this website update.</p><p><a class="btn" href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-vcp-research-update/">Read the research update and evidence →</a></p></aside></div></details></div></li></ul></section><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/">All VSO announcements →</a></p></div></div></main><footer class="site"><div class="wrap">
+<p class="disclosure">Project status (VSO published disclosure, 25 October 2026): zero external implementations · commercial figures withdrawn pending verification (24 October 2026; not a zero-count finding) · zero Evidence Packs accepted in any proceeding.</p>
+<p>VAP is tamper-evident, not tamper-proof — post-hoc evidentiary infrastructure, never runtime control.</p>
